deltaSeconds":503}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":11,"finishersRank":12,"finishRateRank":95,"winningTimeRank":16,"winningTimeRankDir":11,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1959,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"06:28:11"}},"narrative":"The 2014 Comrades Marathon was the 89th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.208 kms. The race was held on Sunday, 1 June. Conditions: Mild cloudless morning. Very hot at midday. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nBongmusa MTHEMBU claimed the men's title in 05:28:34, ahead of Ludwick MAMABOLO (05:33:14) and Gift KELEHE (05:34:39). Eleanor GREENWOOD won the women's race in 06:18:15, followed by Elena NURGALIEVA (06:23:18).\n\nEleanor GREENWOOD's 06:18:15 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1959 (Trevor ALLEN, 06:28:11).\n\nFrom a field of 20,310 entries, 12,006 runners crossed the finish line (59.1% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,567 men and 2,439 women (20.3% female). The average finish time was 10:20:16.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 13 Wally Hayward, 490 Silver, 1,816 Bill Rowan, 5,127 Bronze, 4,540 Vic Clapham. 2,989 runners (24.9%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Michelle DICKENS in 12:00:00.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 55% of the finishers, with 5,397 seniors (avg 10:07:52) and 6,609 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}